*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
# Environment files. The previous list named only `.env` and `.env.local`, so
# `.env.vercel` was committed in Oct 2025 carrying three live third-party
# credentials, one of them valid to 2035. All three have since been revoked,
# but the blob is still reachable in git history. That is the reason this
# pattern matches the whole family instead of naming individual files: a new
# `.env.<something>` must be ignored by default, not by remembering to add it.
# The checked-in example is allowed back explicitly.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
node_modules/

# Ignore markdown files across the repo while keeping the top-level README.md and docs folder tracked
**/*.md
!README.md
!docs/**/*.md

# Local Netlify folder
.netlify

# Playwright output. e2e/.artifacts holds traces and screenshots from failed
# runs and is written by playwright.config.ts `outputDir`; a single trace.zip
# is around 11 MB, so committing them would bloat history for output that is
# only meaningful next to the run that produced it.
e2e/.artifacts/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright/

# Mobile app build artifacts (not deploying mobile version)
apps/mobile/dist/
apps/mobile/.expo/
apps/mobile/node_modules/
*.expo
.expo-shared/
branch_structure.json
temp_auto_push.bat
temp_interactive_push.bat
*.tsbuildinfo

# Vercel project linkage. Deployment is Azure Container Apps only; a
# committed .vercel/project.json re-links the repo to a Vercel project.
.vercel
